WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.539
The Leader/Followers concurrency pattern coordinates
a pool of threads waiting for events.

00:00:05.539 --> 00:00:11.570
One thread leads by waiting on an event source; when
an event arrives, another follower can become

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.648
leader while the previous leader handles the work.

00:00:14.648 --> 00:00:20.617
The purpose is efficient event dispatch with
controlled coordination overhead, not replication of

00:00:20.617 --> 00:00:23.202
durable data across a cluster of machines.

00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:27.647
Kafka illustrates a different use of leader and
follower terminology.

00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:33.767
A partition has a leader responsible for its log
operations and replica followers that copy its

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.089
data.

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:38.598
Leadership can move after failure under a cluster
coordination policy.

00:00:38.598 --> 00:00:44.846
Several partitions can distribute leadership across
brokers, so one leader per partition does not

00:00:44.846 --> 00:00:48.067
mean the entire system has only one active writer.
